cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Fixed-seed RNG confound in Jericho LLM-agent evaluations —
  reproduction artifacts
message: >-
  If you use these artifacts, please cite the methods note. Cite this
  repository's archived release when you need to refer to the data itself.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bahgat Shehata
    given-names: Alessandro
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5353-9081
repository-code: https://github.com/abahgat/jericho-seed-confound
abstract: >-
  Model-free demonstrations and committed artifacts for a methods note reporting
  that Jericho's environment constructor, called without an explicit seed,
  silently binds each game's fixed walkthrough seed. Runs presented as
  independent samples then share one frozen RNG realization. Includes the
  seed-axis and path-axis demonstrations, their machine-readable results for two
  engine versions, tests that re-derive every tabled claim from those results
  without the engine, and the field-level screen of public FrotzEnv call sites.
keywords:
  - jericho
  - interactive fiction
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark evaluation
  - random seeds
  - LLM agents
# Matches the Zenodo deposit: the data is the citable substance. Code is MIT.
license: CC-BY-4.0
# Zenodo mints the DOI from the GitHub release, so this version must equal the
# release tag; a mismatch lands on the archived record.
version: v1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-14'
